  "system": "You review Python code for object-level authorization (access control on a specific object).\nYou are given an access policy, the name of a target function, and some source code.\nDecide whether the target function, as written, lets a requester obtain or disclose an object's data in a way the policy forbids.\n\nRules:\n- Judge only from the code shown. Do not assume authorization logic that is not visible.\n- An `if` statement, or a name containing words such as \"owner\", \"check\", \"guard\" or \"auth\", is not evidence by itself. Confirm what is actually compared, with which values, and what happens when the comparison fails.\n- A call whose return value is ignored does not block anything unless the called code itself raises or stops execution.\n- Data that is returned, yielded, written, appended or sent before a failing check has already been disclosed.\n- If deciding requires code that is not shown (for example a called function whose body is missing), answer \"insufficient_context\" and name what is missing.\n- If the policy allows the access, it is not a problem.\n\nVerdict values:\n- \"vulnerable\": the visible code lets a requester access or disclose data against the policy.\n- \"no_issue_found\": the visible code enforces the policy for the target function.\n- \"insufficient_context\": the decision depends on code that is not shown.\n\nReply with JSON only: {\"verdict\": ..., \"evidence\": ..., \"missing_context\": [...]}.\n\"evidence\" quotes the relevant code lines and explains them briefly. \"missing_context\" lists the missing information (empty list if none).",
  "prompt": "ACCESS POLICY:\nA user profile (name, email, department, role) may be viewed only by that user.\n\nENDPOINT: GET /users/{user_id}/profile\nTARGET FUNCTION: app.routers.users.get_user_profile (the handler of this endpoint)\n\nCODE:\n```python\n# file: app/auth.py\ndef get_current_user(credentials: HTTPAuthorizationCredentials=Depends(bearer_scheme), db: Session=Depends(get_db)) -> User:\n    user = db.get(User, credentials.credentials)\n    if user is None:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED, detail='Invalid token')\n    return user\n\n# file: app/database.py\ndef get_db():\n    db = SessionLocal()\n    try:\n        yield db\n    finally:\n        db.close()\n\n# file: app/routers/users.py\n@router.get('/users/{user_id}/profile', response_model=UserProfile)\ndef get_user_profile(user_id: str, current_user: User=Depends(get_current_user), db: Session=Depends(get_db)):\n    user = db.get(User, user_id)\n    if user is None:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail='User not found')\n    return user\n```\n\nCONTEXT NOTE:\nOnly selected functions from the codebase are shown. Classes (including data models and schemas) and module-level variables are not shown.\nCalls not shown:\n- db.get(...) called in app.auth.get_current_user: not resolved by the extractor (attribute_call), body not shown\n- HTTPException(...) called in app.auth.get_current_user: not resolved by the extractor (imported), body not shown\n- bearer_scheme(...) called in app.auth.get_current_user: not resolved by the extractor (depends_unresolved), body not shown\n- SessionLocal(...) called in app.database.get_db: not resolved by the extractor (module_variable), body not shown\n- db.close(...) called in app.database.get_db: not resolved by the extractor (attribute_call), body not shown\n- db.get(...) called in app.routers.users.get_user_profile: not resolved by the extractor (attribute_call), body not shown\n- HTTPException(...) called in app.routers.users.get_user_profile: not resolved by the extractor (imported), body not shown\n\nReturn the JSON object.",
